id: pm-review-sdk-gap
title: Follow up SDK schemaAddField type forwarding
description: The pinned SDK helper drops the type option. pm-review uses the public schema action fieldType instead; numeric and boolean round trips are covered.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-12T11:24:57.849Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-12T13:33:47.717Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Coordinate a separately authorized upstream helper correction; retain public-action compatibility and real SDK field round-trip regressions.
parent: pm-review-epic
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T11:24:59.623Z",codex-sol,"Observed with SDK 2026.10.10. PmClient.schemaAddField(name, { type: number or boolean }) persists string. client.run(schema, { name, options: { subcommand: add-field, fieldType } }) correctly persists the requested type. This package has a tested workaround; upstream correction is outside this task. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-12T11:33:15.544Z",codex-sol,"Additional environment boundary: normal host strict health reports an unrelated globally installed pm-github SDK requirement 2026.10.11 versus this package pinned host 2026.10.10. Package integrity, storage, locks, settings and history checks pass. The global extension and upstream repos are outside the authorized package scope; isolated-home CI health is checked separately."
  "2026-10-12T13:21:57.091Z",codex-sol,"Upstream schemaAddField drops the supplied type; reproduced on 2026.10.12 and tracked at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1450. Package continues using its existing schema workaround."
